{"author":{"id":"a3a282966ced55effb4560271fcd98e13241af24ea76b00ec76a0f18154bc8ee"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1790620593,"nonce":"ZsO4Zaz+B6lVLnkGsPYAfITrGi8=","message":"2026-09-28 (Luis: \"do it now\"): the query on the unfolded call line is formatted by a real formatter, `jq.Format` in query/jq, a width-aware printer over gojq's syntax tree. Rule: every node on one line where it fits; top-level pipes one stage per line always; what does not fit breaks at its own seam (call → one argument per line, object → one key per line, comma → one item per line, if/try/reduce/foreach in keyword shape). Display only: the parser drops comments and spelling, so when the call line becomes editable the typed text is what is edited and formatting is an action. Unparsable text falls back to the top-level-pipe scanner.","files":null}]}